direction: right
title: Key Salting Technique for Skew Mitigation

FactSide: Skewed Fact Table (Random Salting K=4) {
  style.stroke: "#EF4444"
  SkewRow: Skewed Row: Key = 'NULL' (50M rows)
  SaltGen: concat(key, '_', floor(rand() * 4))
  Buckets: Produces 4 Even Buckets ('NULL_0' .. 'NULL_3')
  SkewRow -> SaltGen -> Buckets
}

DimSide: Small Dimension Table (Explode K=4) {
  style.stroke: "#34D399"
  DimRow: Dimension Row: Key = 'NULL'
  Explode: explode(array(0, 1, 2, 3))
  RepRows: 4 Replicated Rows ('NULL_0' .. 'NULL_3')
  DimRow -> Explode -> RepRows
}

BalancedJoin: Balanced Join Across 4 Workers {
  style.stroke: "#34D399"
}

FactSide.Buckets -> BalancedJoin: Even 12.5M partitions { style.stroke: "#34D399" }
DimSide.RepRows -> BalancedJoin: Matched replicated keys { style.stroke: "#34D399" }
